        "\"\"\"\n",
        "MODULE 09 LAB: ENSEMBLE METHODS (IRIS DATASET)\n",
        "\n",
        "OBJECTIVE:\n",
        "Understand why combining multiple models leads to more accurate\n",
        "and reliable predictions than using a single model.\n",
        "\n",
        "CORE IDEA:\n",
        "A single Decision Tree can \"overreact\" to noise.\n",
        "A Random Forest reduces this by combining many trees.\n",
        "\n",
        "We will:\n",
        "1. Train a single Decision Tree (baseline)\n",
        "2. Observe its limitations (overfitting / bias)\n",
        "3. Introduce randomness (bootstrapping)\n",
        "4. Build a Random Forest\n",
        "5. Compare performance\n",
        "\n",
        "GUIDING QUESTION:\n",
        "Why does a group of imperfect models outperform one \"perfect\" model?\n",
        "\"\"\""
      ],
      "id": "0q5dx_Exd88u"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "iwzqT_AQd88y"
      },
      "source": [
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "PART 1: THE WISDOM OF THE CROWD\n",
        "\n",
        "Instead of relying on one Decision Tree,\n",
        "we combine multiple trees into a \"committee.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "Each tree sees the Iris data slightly differently.\n",
        "Their combined vote is more stable than any single tree.\n",
        "\n",
        "KEY IDEA:\n",
        "- One tree = high variance or bias\n",
        "- Many trees = balanced, more reliable prediction\n",
        "\"\"\""
      ],
      "id": "iwzqT_AQd88y"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# --- DATA (Iris: 2 features for visualization) ---\n",
        "from sklearn.datasets import load_iris\n",
        "from sklearn.tree import DecisionTreeClassifier\n",
        "from sklearn.ensemble import VotingClassifier\n",
        "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "iris = load_iris()\n",
        "features = iris.data[:, :2]  # Sepal only (for 2D)\n",
        "labels = iris.target\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n",
        "    features, labels, test_size=0.3, random_state=42\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# --- MODELS (Create diversity intentionally) ---\n",
        "tree_a = DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=2, random_state=1)\n",
        "tree_b = DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=3, random_state=2)\n",
        "tree_c = DecisionTreeClassifier(max_depth=4, random_state=3)\n",
        "\n",
        "ensemble = VotingClassifier(\n",
        "    estimators=[('a', tree_a), ('b', tree_b), ('c', tree_c)],\n",
        "    voting='hard'\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Train all\n",
        "for model in [tree_a, tree_b, tree_c, ensemble]:\n",
        "    model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n",
        "\n",
        "    ax1.set_title(\"Single Tree: Limited Perspective\")\n",
        "\n",
        "ax2.set_title(\"Ensemble: Combined Perspective\")\n",
        "\n",
        "\"LIMITATION:\\nA single tree makes decisions\\nbased on limited patterns.\\nThis can miss the full structure.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "\"LIMITATION:\\nA single tree makes decisions\\nbased on limited patterns.\\nThis can miss the full structure.\""
